From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:34:49 +0200
Subject: media: sun6i-isp: Give the active mbus format a default

The active format on the processor's sink pad is only ever assigned by
set_fmt, so until userspace configures the subdev it reads back as
zeroes. Everything that consults it gets those zeroes: the optical black
registers end up describing a frame of no size, and the input format
lookup falls through its WARN_ON.

Only the TRY format was being initialised, in init_state. Pull those
defaults into a helper and apply them to the active format at setup
time as well.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_proc.c | 25 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_proc.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_proc.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_proc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_proc.c
@@ -329,6 +329,16 @@ sun6i_isp_proc_mbus_format_prepare(struct v4l2_mbus_framefmt *mbus_format)
 	mbus_format->xfer_func = V4L2_XFER_FUNC_DEFAULT;
 }
 
+static void
+sun6i_isp_proc_mbus_format_default(struct v4l2_mbus_framefmt *mbus_format)
+{
+	mbus_format->code = sun6i_isp_proc_formats[0].mbus_code;
+	mbus_format->width = 1280;
+	mbus_format->height = 720;
+
+	sun6i_isp_proc_mbus_format_prepare(mbus_format);
+}
+
 static int sun6i_isp_proc_init_state(struct v4l2_subdev *subdev,
 				     struct v4l2_subdev_state *state)
 {
@@ -340,11 +350,7 @@ static int sun6i_isp_proc_init_state(struct v4l2_subdev *subdev,
 
 	mutex_lock(lock);
 
-	mbus_format->code = sun6i_isp_proc_formats[0].mbus_code;
-	mbus_format->width = 1280;
-	mbus_format->height = 720;
-
-	sun6i_isp_proc_mbus_format_prepare(mbus_format);
+	sun6i_isp_proc_mbus_format_default(mbus_format);
 
 	mutex_unlock(lock);
 
@@ -574,6 +580,15 @@ int sun6i_isp_proc_setup(struct sun6i_isp_device *isp_dev)
 
 	mutex_init(&proc->lock);
 
+	/*
+	 * The active format is only ever assigned by set_fmt, so without
+	 * this everything reading it back -- the optical black geometry, the
+	 * input format, the bound on the capture size -- would see zeroes
+	 * until userspace configured the subdev.
+	 */
+
+	sun6i_isp_proc_mbus_format_default(&proc->mbus_format);
+
 	/* V4L2 Subdev */
 
 	v4l2_subdev_init(subdev, &sun6i_isp_proc_subdev_ops);
-- 
Armbian

